# Byte parity across operating systems.
#
# The conformance suite compares rendered recipe text against the canonical
# files in recipes/ byte for byte, and the Go SDK embeds copies of those
# files at compile time. A CRLF-converting checkout (the default on Windows
# runners) would corrupt those comparisons, so every text file checks out
# with LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Gradle wrapper batch script is consumed by cmd.exe and keeps its
# committed bytes untouched.
*.bat -text

# The pre-schema ingestion boundary's fixtures are byte fixtures: byte order
# marks, UTF-16 and UTF-32 documents, deliberately malformed UTF-8, and
# documents whose exact byte length is the thing under test. Line-ending
# normalisation would rewrite the bytes these fixtures exist to pin.
conformance/fixtures/boundary/** -text
